Library     ../python/config_validator/config_validator.py  WITH NAME  config_validator

Resource    HWPTA_Logger.robot


*** Keywords ***
Switch from default init to suite custom init
    [Documentation]    Switches from default testline configuration (usually provided via `robot -V /path/to/init`) to suite custom testline configuration provided during Suite Setup.
    ...                If suite custom testline configuration is None, then keeps using default testline configuration.
    ...                If validation is enabled, validates default and suite custom (if provided) testline configurations.
    ...                Make sure that suite custom testline configuration is a subset of default testline configuration if validation is enabled.
    [Arguments]        ${custom_tl}=${None}
    ...                ${validate}=${True}

    Set global variable                            ${default_tl}
    ...                                            ${tl}

    IF  ${validate}
        config_validator.validate_default_init     default_tl=${default_tl}
    END

    IF  $custom_tl is not None
        Set global variable                        ${suite_custom_tl}
        ...                                        ${custom_tl}

        IF  ${validate}
            config_validator.validate_custom_init  default_tl=${default_tl}
            ...                                    custom_tl=${suite_custom_tl}
        END

        Robot log warning                          Switching from default init to suite custom init
        Set global variable                        ${tl}
        ...                                        ${suite_custom_tl}
    ELSE
        Set global variable                        ${suite_custom_tl}
        ...                                        ${None}
    END

Switch from current init to test custom init
    [Documentation]    Switches from current testline configuration (suite custom if was used, otherwise default) to test custom testline configuration provided during Test Setup.
    ...                If test custom testline configuration is None, then keeps using current testline configuration.
    ...                If validation is enabled and test custom testline configuration is provided, validates test custom testline configuration.
    ...                Make sure that test custom testline configuration is a subset of default testline configuration (usually provided via `robot -V /path/to/init`) if validation is enabled.
    [Arguments]        ${custom_tl}=${None}
    ...                ${validate}=${True}

    IF  $custom_tl is not None
        Set global variable                        ${test_custom_tl}
        ...                                        ${custom_tl}

        IF  ${validate}
            config_validator.validate_custom_init  default_tl=${default_tl}
            ...                                    custom_tl=${test_custom_tl}
        END

        IF  $suite_custom_tl is not None
            Robot log warning                      Switching from suite custom init to test custom init
        ELSE
            Robot log warning                      Switching from default init to test custom init
        END

        Set global variable                        ${tl}
        ...                                        ${test_custom_tl}
    ELSE
        Set global variable                        ${test_custom_tl}
        ...                                        ${None}
    END

Switch from test custom init to previous init
    [Documentation]    Switches from test custom testline configuration, provided during Test Setup, to previous testline configuration (suite custom if was used, otherwise default).

    IF  $test_custom_tl is not None
        IF  $suite_custom_tl is not None
            Robot log warning             Switching from test custom init to suite custom init
            Set global variable           ${tl}
            ...                           ${suite_custom_tl}
        ELSE
            Robot log warning             Switching from test custom init to default init
            Set global variable           ${tl}
            ...                           ${default_tl}
        END

        Set global variable               ${test_custom_tl}
        ...                               ${None}
    END
